      "With the preceding chains of narration, from Ali ibn Mahzyar... from Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari, who said:",
      "The Messenger of Allah addressed us, praised Allah, then said: \"O people — adhere to prayer, for it is the pillar of your religion. Strive during the night with prayer and remember Allah abundantly. The example of these five prayers is a flowing river near your door, in which you bathe five times daily. Just as bathing cleanses the body, constant prayer cleanses sins until nothing remains.",
      "O people, there is no servant except that he is bound with knotted straps. When two-thirds of the night has passed and one-third remains, an angel comes and says: 'Rise and remember Allah, for the dawn is near.' If he stirs and remembers Allah, one knot is undone. If he rises, performs wudu and enters prayer, all knots are undone, and he enters the morning with joy in his eyes.\""
